#AI:1
TYPE="path_rules"
GLOB="ai_context/**, ai_modules/**, readme_AI.ai, AI_HANDOFF.ai, WORKSHEET.heywy, SIDEQUESTS.ai"

PURPOSE:
Rules active when editing AI continuity files. Loaded on demand when these
paths are touched. These rules protect continuity integrity across sessions.

---

IMMUTABLE_RULES:
- Append only. Do not rewrite history in any .ai or .heywy file.
- Do not modify USAGE or STATE sections of readme_AI.ai unless explicitly instructed.
- Do not delete entries from AI_HANDOFF.ai — move oldest to HANDOFF_ARCHIVE section if needed.
- Do not delete entries from ai_context/decision_log.md — mark SUPERSEDED instead.
- Do not delete DEC-NNN, EXP-NNN, or CLAR-NNN entries from readme_AI_archive.ai — historical record.
- Closed THREADS move from readme_AI.ai THREADS to readme_AI_archive.ai with a closure summary line.

---

ENTRY_NUMBERING:
- THR-NNN — work threads, opened sequentially in readme_AI.ai THREADS section
- DEC-NNN — decisions, opened sequentially in ai_context/decision_log.md (mirrored to readme_AI_archive on finalize)
- EXP-NNN — experiments, opened sequentially in readme_AI.ai RECENT_EXPERIMENTS (overflow to archive after 6 entries)
- CLAR-NNN — clarifications/corrections, appended to readme_AI_archive.ai when an earlier entry needs correction (use CLAR instead of rewriting EXP/DEC/THR)
- Never reuse a retired number. Skipped numbers stay skipped (document the skip in the next entry's body if useful).

---

WRITEBACK_TARGETS:
- New THREAD or active THREAD update → readme_AI.ai
- Recent experiments (last 6) → readme_AI.ai RECENT_EXPERIMENTS
- Older experiments (overflow from 6) → ai_context/readme_AI_archive.ai EXPERIMENTS
- Decisions made → ai_context/decision_log.md (in-effect) + ai_context/readme_AI_archive.ai DECISIONS (finalized)
- Project state changes → ai_context/current_state.md
- Session end → AI_HANDOFF.ai (append new SESSION-N block)
- Human input handled → WORKSHEET.heywy (move to HISTORY section, do not delete)
- Cross-project parked ideas → SIDEQUESTS.ai (status: parked|active|shipped|dropped)

---

EXPERIMENT_FORMAT (RECENT_EXPERIMENTS):
@YYYY-MM-DD|EXP-NNN|
change="..."
expect="..."
observe="..."
repro="..."         (optional; command or steps to reproduce)
revert="..."        (how to back out if needed)
location="..."      (files/paths affected)
status="passed | failed | partial | reverted"

THREADS_FORMAT:
- THR-NNN|open|closed|paused|blocked|tier=haiku|sonnet|opus|"short description"
- Order by ID. New threads append at bottom.
- Status changes are edits in place (not appends).

DECISION_FORMAT (decision_log.md):
@YYYY-MM-DD|DEC-NNN|"short title"
rationale="..."
impact="..."
status="active | superseded by DEC-MMM"

CLARIFICATION_FORMAT (readme_AI_archive.ai):
@YYYY-MM-DD|CLAR-NNN|corrects=EXP-NNN|DEC-NNN|THR-NNN
issue="what was wrong or unclear"
correction="what is actually true"
evidence="how we know"

---

SIDEQUESTS_USAGE:
SIDEQUESTS.ai is for ideas that came up during work but don't belong to the current project's THREADS. Each entry has a status:
- parked   — captured, no decision yet
- active   — being explored in parallel (rare; usually means it should be a THR)
- shipped  — promoted to a real project or merged elsewhere
- dropped  — explicitly decided against (include one-line reason)

Promote a sidequest to a THR when it has a concrete owner, scope, and acceptance criteria. Drop a sidequest when it conflicts with project direction or duplicates existing work — never silently delete.

---

FILE_TYPE_REMINDER:
- .ai — AI-facing. Human should not need to read these. Exception: readme_AI.ai is the project cartridge.
- .heywy — Human-facing. AI reads but does not own direction. WORKSHEET.heywy is the human input channel.

---

SUBSTRATE_CODE_CONSISTENCY:
; drift-sweep's mission-freshness check enforces the time thresholds below.
- When code changes direction, update ai_context/CURRENT_MISSION.md before the next session. Substrate describes intent; code describes implementation. They must not diverge for more than MISSION_STALE_DAYS (default 14).
- When a THREAD closes or is superseded, update its status in readme_AI.ai immediately. Ghost threads (open status on completed work) are substrate drift.
- After a probe cycle, capture findings in RECENT_EXPERIMENTS or decision_log.md before ending the session. Findings left only in code comments rot when the surrounding code changes.
- If code was touched and substrate was not, that is expected. If substrate was updated without corresponding code change, verify the substrate reflects current code reality — do not update substrate to match a plan that was not executed.

---

NON_NEGOTIABLES:
- Continuity files are the source of truth for what's been tried, decided, and built.
  Do not act on assumptions when continuity files have the answer — read them first.
- If a continuity entry shows a closed or SUPERSEDED decision, do not silently reopen it.
  Surface the conflict via STOP-THE-LINE before re-attempting.
